  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by virtue of its scale and siting on the public footpath, would reduce the available footpath in an area of high footfall where the full width of the remaining footpath is considered necessary for pedestrians. This is considered harmful to users of the public highway, particularly in the sense of pedestrian movements, and is therefore contrary to the objectives of Policy 60 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024), which seeks to protect the walking and cycling environment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Given its appearance and siting the proposed development would add to a general cluttering of the streetscene in an area which is already noted to host considerable street furniture and other infrastructure of various scales. This is considered harmful to the visual amenity of the immediate area and therefore fails to comply with the objectives of Policy 53 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024) and Policy D8 of the London Plan (2021).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
